d-borne proper adding another  unexpected layer to Garmin's mysterious  past like many of the other weapons in  this expansion this safe space stats  don't deviate far from the arms and the  main game the same goes for the fists of  karate a crude hunk of iron that  effectively functions as a brass knuckle  in the ranges weapons slot while the  safe essentially functions like a stock  leaver you'll find nuance in the speed  of the combos with your hunter's arms  stretching a bit further with each swing  compared to the immediacy of the attack  from the sake alternatively you can now  wield a giant circular saw known as the  whirligig saw which attaches to an  almost equally lethal bent step aside  from being viable alternatives to the  flagship weapons it's intriguing to see  how these new tools work in action  [Music]  for as disturbing and depressing as  yharnam is in blood-borne it felt like  the dark city still had a chance at  redemption the version of this city in  the old hunters is beyond salvation all  the familiar paths are now covered in  what appears to be hardened dough with  fingerprint like lines and ridges  scrawled through them countless gallons  of blood drenched the lower areas  leaving you to wonder what in the world  happened since the last time you visited  the doom city the answer might be in the  broken sky above knowledge of the games  full maps and shortcuts are of no value  here so despite that you can recognize  many of the landmarks and yharnam none  of blood-borne 's previous locales feel  reused and instead offer new challenges  for devoted hunters the old hunters is  blood borne from another time in place  and with more difficult bosses and  confounding stories to unravel it's also  a great complement to the original  gruesome adventure  [Music]  you
 

